+## Review-8aee66b709b13528 — same-color panel shortcut
+
+A reusable source-pinned protected-Racket probe was added at `workspace/probe_same_color_shortcut.py`. Ordinary generation always assigns distinct nonzero colors to the two panels, while `self_check` accepts lawful same-color panels. Consequently the executable shortcut “OR for different panel colors, AND for the same panel color” fits all three ordinary demonstrations at seed 41. Recoloring the query’s right panel to the left panel color preserves structural validity and the canonical OR label, but the shortcut changes six cells.
+
+Suggested repair: admit same-color panels into ordinary lessons, or add this competitor and reject lessons until a visible same-color OR witness refutes it. Production remains unchanged; this is one bounded source-bound witness, not a universal census. Evidence: `checks/d7068a5d39a2/same-color-shortcut.json`.
